From 838f95ee633ad98783c7323deab6d5bcad4736e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeUnitOPS <ops@freeunit.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:19:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bench: queue the post-release server bisect, and record a
 named arm's commit

The range b09815f1..33896f7e is 26 commits and only its ends are measured, so
"the server went up" has no bisect and no release baseline on hello -- the one
cell where the server layer is the whole request.

128 splits the range at 1f7511a3, its only core commit; 124 is the missing
release baseline.  Their images are built by build-images.sh, and the two jobs
run in scripts/campaign.steps.bisect-server.

A master-<sha> arm published :master's sha instead of its own: run 118 names
b09815f1 and ff694772 while both arms ran master-33896f7, which reads as one
build across two hosts when it is not even the same image.  run.sh now writes
runtime_a_commit/runtime_a_image for a named-commit arm beside the image id.

OPS-Agent: DeepSeek Flash
